WEBVTT

00:00:01.659 --> 00:00:09.127
Collateral & Pledges
The security behind every loan — what it is worth, what it lends, and what happens when its value falls.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:17.520
Jean-Marc Lagesse is borrowing MUR 9.45M to buy a construction lot
The lot itself will secure the loan — the loans executive registers it

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:24.680
Sign in as Sophie Lagesse — Loans Executive
The loans executive handles the loan and its security

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:31.080
Collateral & Pledges ▸ Collateral Register ▸ New
Link it to the loan application — leave Owner empty when the borrower owns it

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:38.320
The value from the sale agreement — the bank's own valuation follows
Leave Haircut empty: the standard haircut for the type applies

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:46.600
Land carries a standard 10% haircut, from Masters ▸ Collateral types
The master also sets the revaluation frequency and the LTV levels

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:52.960
Lending value = market value less the haircut: MUR 9.45M
Exactly the loan amount

00:00:52.960 --> 00:01:06.920
Collateral Allocations: how much of the security backs which loan
One property can secure several loans or facilities — each gets its share

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:15.600
On the loan application, the security lending value now shows MUR 9.45M
It adds up the lending value of every collateral registered for the loan

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:24.280
At Security & insurance the team completes valuation, notary, charge and insurance
Ready for disbursement stays blocked until “Security complete” is Yes

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:33.200
The bank's panel valuer reports — the credit analyst records it
Collateral Valuations ▸ New: date, market value, forced-sale value, valuer

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:50.120
Sign in as Nadia Peerbux — Credit Analyst
The credit analyst checks the security

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:58.040
The latest valuation becomes the market value — lending value is now MUR 9.72M
The loan stays covered with room to spare

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:04.760
Next revaluation: three years for land, from the master
A reminder goes to the owner of the record on the day it falls due

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:13.440
Insured property: 30 days before the cover lapses, a reminder goes out
Here the building policy expires on 1 November — flagged as lapsing

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:23.960
Investment-backed loan: Lina Chan borrowed against her fund units
MUR 1.14M outstanding — secured by a pledge of Genesis Foreign Equity Fund units

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:31.720
LTV = drawn exposure ÷ market value of the registered pledges
Today 7.3% — her whole holding is pledged

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:39.800
Margin-call level 80%, liquidation 90% — per asset class, from the master
Checked again every time a pledge is revalued

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:46.680
Sign in as Ritesh Seewoo — Operations Checker
Operations registers and releases pledges with the transfer agent

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:55.720
Lina is redeeming most of her units — the pledge keeps only 3,600
Enough to cover the loan after the 30% haircut

00:02:55.720 --> 00:03:05.640
3,600 units at the latest NAV: MUR 1.62M
The loan's LTV is recalculated at once: 70.8% — still within limits

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:19.320
A month later equity markets fall — the units lose 14%
Operations records the monthly market-price valuation of the pledge

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:28.200
The LTV is now above 80% — the CRM raises a margin call by itself
No one has to spot it: the check runs the moment the pledge is revalued

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:38.840
LTV 82.2% — margin call, with the shortfall to restore cover
Shortfall = drawn exposure less the pledges' lending value

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:50.200
Margin call MC-2026-000012: LTV at call, shortfall, cure within five business days
Assigned to the loans manager · Lina is emailed and texted

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:56.160
Docs: the margin-call notice letter, generated in Lina's language
The same notice was emailed to her

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:01.920
The loans manager calls Lina
Margin Calls pipeline: Issued ▸ Client contacted ▸ Cured / Liquidation

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:13.720
Sign in as Rajiv Doorgakant — Manager, Loans & Fixed Income
Margin calls are routed to the loans manager

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:20.560
Lina will pledge more units rather than repay — try closing the call now…
Cured needs to know how the call was cured

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:25.560
Blocked: record how the call was cured first
Additional collateral or a partial repayment

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:34.240
Operations registers the extra pledge: units of her money-market fund
Collateral Register ▸ New — fund units, pledge registered with the transfer agent

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:40.960
Sign in as Ritesh Seewoo — Operations Checker
Operations registers the new pledge

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:55.720
Collateral Register ▸ New: fund units, linked to Lina's loan
4,000 units of her money-market fund, pledge registered

00:04:55.720 --> 00:05:03.520
LTV back to 63% — within limits, no shortfall
The extra units restored the cover

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:11.400
Operations records the cure on the margin call
Cure: Additional collateral

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:16.080
Now the call can move to Cured
The cure is recorded, so the gate lets it through

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:20.080
Cured within the deadline — the call is closed
A new call is raised if the LTV passes the call level again

00:05:22.084 --> 00:05:29.640
Collateral & Pledges
Staff register and value the security — the CRM keeps lending value and LTV current and raises the alarms.
